   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "PS7_001_Function Spread Of Marks",
   "display_name": "Spread Of Marks",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A teacher wants to know how spread out the marks of a class are. A simple measure is the <b>spread</b>: the highest mark minus the lowest mark.</p>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>len(L)</code>, <code>sum(L)</code>, <code>min(L)</code>, <code>max(L)</code>, <code>sorted(L)</code> (a new sorted list; <code>sorted(L, reverse=True)</code> sorts from largest to smallest), <code>L.count(x)</code>, <code>L.index(x)</code>, <code>L.append(x)</code>, slices.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>spread(marks)</code> that takes a non-empty list of integers <code>marks</code> and <b>returns</b> the highest mark minus the lowest mark.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>spread([45, 80, 62, 91])</code> returns <code>46</code> (91 - 45)</li><li><code>spread([70, 70, 70])</code> returns <code>0</code> (everybody got the same)</li><li><code>spread([5])</code> returns <code>0</code></li></ul>",
   "answerpreload": "def spread(marks):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(spread([45, 80, 62, 91]))\n",
