   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "PS7_002_Function Count Above Average",
   "display_name": "Count Above Average",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>average</b> of a list of numbers is their sum divided by how many there are: <code>sum(L) / len(L)</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>len(L)</code>, <code>sum(L)</code>, <code>min(L)</code>, <code>max(L)</code>, <code>sorted(L)</code> (a new sorted list; <code>sorted(L, reverse=True)</code> sorts from largest to smallest), <code>L.count(x)</code>, <code>L.index(x)</code>, <code>L.append(x)</code>, slices.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>count_above_average(L)</code> that takes a non-empty list of integers <code>L</code> and <b>returns</b> how many items are <b>strictly greater</b> than the average.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>count_above_average([2, 4, 6, 8])</code> returns <code>2</code> (the average is 5.0; 6 and 8 are above it)</li><li><code>count_above_average([5, 5, 5])</code> returns <code>0</code> (the average is 5.0; nothing is strictly above it)</li><li><code>count_above_average([1, 1, 1, 9])</code> returns <code>1</code></li></ul>",
   "answerpreload": "def count_above_average(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(count_above_average([2, 4, 6, 8]))\n",
