   "xml_name": "PS7_003_Function Top Three Scores",
   "display_name": "Top Three Scores",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>In a quiz contest, the three highest scores win prizes.</p>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>len(L)</code>, <code>sum(L)</code>, <code>min(L)</code>, <code>max(L)</code>, <code>sorted(L)</code> (a new sorted list; <code>sorted(L, reverse=True)</code> sorts from largest to smallest), <code>L.count(x)</code>, <code>L.index(x)</code>, <code>L.append(x)</code>, slices.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>top_three(scores)</code> that takes a list of integers <code>scores</code> and <b>returns</b> a new list with the three highest scores, from highest to lowest. If there are fewer than three scores, return all of them, from highest to lowest. Equal scores are kept (two people may have the same score). Do not change <code>scores</code> itself.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>top_three([40, 95, 70, 88, 60])</code> returns <code>[95, 88, 70]</code></li><li><code>top_three([50, 90, 90, 20])</code> returns <code>[90, 90, 50]</code></li><li><code>top_three([12, 30])</code> returns <code>[30, 12]</code></li></ul>",
