  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "PS7_007_Function Best So Far",
   "display_name": "Best So Far",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A shop records its sales every day. The owner wants to see, for each day, the <b>best day so far</b>: the highest sale from the first day up to and including that day.</p>\n<pre>sales:        [3, 7, 5, 9, 2]\nbest so far:  [3, 7, 7, 9, 9]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>best_so_far(L)</code> that takes a list of integers <code>L</code> and <b>returns</b> a new list of the same length, where the item at index <code>i</code> is the largest of <code>L[0]</code>, <code>L[1]</code>, ..., <code>L[i]</code>. An empty <code>L</code> gives an empty list.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>best_so_far([3, 7, 5, 9, 2])</code> returns <code>[3, 7, 7, 9, 9]</code></li><li><code>best_so_far([5, 4, 3])</code> returns <code>[5, 5, 5]</code></li><li><code>best_so_far([])</code> returns <code>[]</code></li></ul>",
   "answerpreload": "def best_so_far(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your code; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(best_so_far([3, 7, 5, 9, 2]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(best_so_far([3, 7, 5, 9, 2]))",
