   "display_name": "Column Total",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <b>table</b> can be stored as a list of rows, where each row is a list. <code>table[r][c]</code> is the item in row <code>r</code>, column <code>c</code>:</p>\n<pre>table = [[3, 1, 4],\n         [1, 5, 9],\n         [2, 6, 5]]</pre>\n<p>Here <code>table[1]</code> is the whole row <code>[1, 5, 9]</code>, and <code>table[1][2]</code> is <code>9</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>column_total(table, c)</code> that <b>returns</b> the sum of the items in column <code>c</code> of the table (one item from every row). All rows have the same length, and <code>c</code> is a valid column index. A table with no rows gives <code>0</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>column_total([[3, 1, 4], [1, 5, 9], [2, 6, 5]], 0)</code> returns <code>6</code> (3 + 1 + 2)</li><li><code>column_total([[3, 1, 4], [1, 5, 9], [2, 6, 5]], 2)</code> returns <code>18</code> (4 + 9 + 5)</li><li><code>column_total([[7, 8]], 1)</code> returns <code>8</code></li></ul>",
