   "xml_name": "PS7_009_Function Middle Value",
   "display_name": "Middle Value",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>median</b> of a list of numbers is the value in the middle once the numbers are sorted. For example, for <code>[7, 2, 9, 4, 5]</code>, sorting gives <code>[2, 4, 5, 7, 9]</code>, and the middle value is <code>5</code>.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">sorted:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">7</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">5 items: the middle one has index 5 // 2 = 2</div>\n<p><b>Python facts you may use:</b> <code>len(L)</code>, <code>sum(L)</code>, <code>min(L)</code>, <code>max(L)</code>, <code>sorted(L)</code> (a new sorted list; <code>sorted(L, reverse=True)</code> sorts from largest to smallest), <code>L.count(x)</code>, <code>L.index(x)</code>, <code>L.append(x)</code>, slices.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>median(L)</code> that takes a list of integers <code>L</code> with an <b>odd</b> number of items, and <b>returns</b> its median. Do not change <code>L</code> itself.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>median([7, 2, 9, 4, 5])</code> returns <code>5</code></li><li><code>median([3, 1, 2])</code> returns <code>2</code></li><li><code>median([8])</code> returns <code>8</code></li></ul>",
