   "display_name": "Players Older Than",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A list of <b>records</b> can be stored as a list of tuples, one tuple per person. A <code>for</code> loop can unpack each tuple directly:</p>\n<pre>team = [(&quot;Kavya&quot;, 19), (&quot;Arjun&quot;, 22)]\nfor name, age in team:\n    print(name, &quot;is&quot;, age)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>Kavya is 19\nArjun is 22</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a function <code>older_than(team, age)</code> that takes a list of <code>(name, age)</code> tuples and an integer <code>age</code>, and <b>returns</b> a list of the names of the players who are <b>strictly older</b> than <code>age</code>, in the original order.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>older_than([(\"Kavya\", 19), (\"Arjun\", 22), (\"Dev\", 25)], 20)</code> returns <code>['Arjun', 'Dev']</code></li><li><code>older_than([(\"Kavya\", 19)], 19)</code> returns <code>[]</code></li></ul>",
