   "display_name": "Matching Answers With Zip",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>zip(a, b)</code> pairs up the items of two lists, position by position, giving tuples:</p>\n<pre>key = [&quot;A&quot;, &quot;C&quot;, &quot;B&quot;]\nmine = [&quot;A&quot;, &quot;B&quot;, &quot;B&quot;]\nprint(list(zip(key, mine)))\nfor k, m in zip(key, mine):\n    print(k, m, k == m)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[(&#x27;A&#x27;, &#x27;A&#x27;), (&#x27;C&#x27;, &#x27;B&#x27;), (&#x27;B&#x27;, &#x27;B&#x27;)]\nA A True\nC B False\nB B True</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> a quiz has a list of correct answers <code>key</code>, and a student's answers <code>mine</code> (a list of the same length). Write a function <code>score(key, mine)</code> that <b>returns</b> how many of the student's answers match the correct answer at the same position.</p>\n<p><b>Examples:</b></p>\n<ul><li><code>score([\"A\", \"C\", \"B\"], [\"A\", \"B\", \"B\"])</code> returns <code>2</code></li><li><code>score([], [])</code> returns <code>0</code></li></ul>",
